unts of protein  although there are many vegetarian  sources of protein like soy tofu and  oats what's special about moringa  protein is that it is a complete source  of protein meaning it contains all 20  essential amino acids as compared to  many other sources of plant protein  which contains incomplete proteins these  incomplete proteins lack one or other  essential amino acids that cannot be  produced by our body so in that case the  protein present in the moringa plant is  very good for our body powders made from  its crushed leaves are packed with  almost three grams of protein per  tablespoon  number three moringa is good for your  liver health  free radicals are created in our body by  things like pollution fried food sun  exposure drug intake and many other  harmful activities going on in our body  the damage our body by causing oxidative  stress cell damage and premature aging  this damage is especially prominent in  our liver as it is most active site in  our body for the waste removal and free  radical  metabolism the moringa plant contains  abundant antioxidants like flavonoids  polyphenols and ascorbic acid that can  help to reduce the damage that is done  by the free radicals  this promotes liver health and a diet  rich in antioxidants has been shown to  prevent premature aging and wrinkles on  the skin  number four moringa is good for people  with diabetes  moringa helps to reduce the amount of  glucose levels in the blood as well as  the sugar and protein levels in the  urine  spikes in the insulin and blood sugar  levels can lead to development of type 2  diabetes and obesity  according to a scientific study moringa  leaf powder extract has been effective  in reducing the lipid and glucose levels  in patients with diabetes  one clinical study also proved the  therapeutic antioxidant properties of  moringa as well as the lower fasting  glucose levels in post-menopausal women  who took a supplement with moringa and  amaranth leaves for three months  